  "spawn_rules_text": "How spawns work. The server runs a global 7.56s respawn tick across every loaded map. After a mob dies its spawn point waits a cooldown (5s default, or usually the WZ mobTime value for timed spawns), then the mob reappears on the next tick. Field-boss schedules are server-owned, so unconfirmed live-timing windows are labelled when they differ from the raw map value. Map capacity scales with players on the map: 75% solo, +5% per extra player, capping at 100% from 6 players. This map has 34 spawn points, so capacity is ~26 concurrent mobs solo and 34 in a full party. Mob rate (1.2x) multiplies that capacity: expect about 41 monsters up at a time. Not applied to the figures above yet; best reading from closed-beta play.",
  "mob_rate_text": "About mob rate. Mob rate multiplies how many monsters this map keeps alive at once. This map has 34 spawn points and a mob rate of 1.2x, so expect about 41 monsters up at a time instead of 34. The spawn figures above do not apply it yet. This is our best reading from closed-beta play, where a high-rate map held far more monsters than it has spawn points; an exact whole-map count has not been done.",
